  "goodToKnow": "Die Zivilcourage is civil or moral courage: standing up in public for others or for one's values, such as intervening when someone is harassed on a train. It's a key concept in German civic education, linked to the lesson of the Nazi era, when too few spoke up. Police campaigns advise safe ways to show Zivilcourage, like calling 110. Pronounced with French courage: tsi-VEEL-ku-RAA-zhe. It has no plural."
